{"name":"Venus Slipper Orchid","hex":"#df73ff","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"venus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the bivalve molluscs in the genus Venus or family Veneridae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venus"},{"term":"slipper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A low soft shoe that can be slipped on and off easily.","A low soft shoe intended for indoor use; a bedroom slipper or house slipper."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["slippery"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slipper"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cypripedioideae","blocks":[{"text":"Cypripedioideae is a subfamily of orchids commonly known as lady's slipper orchids, lady slipper orchids or slipper orchids. Cypripedioideae includes the genera Cypripedium, Mexipedium, Paphiopedilum, Phragmipedium and Selenipedium. They are characterised by the slipper-shaped pouches of the flowers – the pouch traps insects so they are forced to climb up past the staminode, behind which they collect or deposit pollinia, thus fertilizing the flower. There are approximately 165 species in the subfamily."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Paphiopedilum_2.jpg/330px-Paphiopedilum_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypripedioideae"},{"title":"Paphiopedilum","blocks":[{"text":"Paphiopedilum, often called the Venus slipper, is a genus of the lady slipper orchid subfamily Cypripedioideae of the flowering plant family Orchidaceae. The genus comprises some 80 accepted taxa including several natural hybrids. The genus is native to Southeast Asia, the Indian subcontinent, southern China, New Guinea and the Solomon and Bismarck Islands. The type species of this genus is Paphiopedilum insigne."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Paphiopedilum_henryanum_Orchi_001.jpg/330px-Paphiopedilum_henryanum_Orchi_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paphiopedilum"},{"title":"Venus","blocks":[{"text":"Venus is the second planet from the Sun. Similar in size and mass to Earth, Venus has no liquid water, and its atmosphere is far thicker and denser than that of any other rocky body in the Solar System. The atmosphere is composed mostly of carbon dioxide and has a thick cloud layer of sulfuric acid that spans the whole planet. At the mean surface level, the atmosphere reaches a temperature of 737 K, making it the hottest planet in the solar system and also a pressure 92 times greater than Earth's at sea level, turning the lowest layer of the atmosphere into a supercritical fluid. From Earth, Venus is visible as a star-like point of light, appearing brighter than any other natural point of light in the sky, as either the brightest \"morning star\" or \"evening star\". It was also given the poetic name Ēarendel in Old English, meaning \"ray of light\" along with the two previous epithets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Venus_from_Mariner_10.jpg/330px-Venus_from_Mariner_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus"},{"title":"Slipper","blocks":[{"text":"Slippers are a type of shoes falling under the broader category of light footwear, that are easy to put on and off and are intended to be worn indoors, particularly at home. They provide comfort and protection for the feet when walking indoors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Slippers.jpg/330px-Slippers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slipper"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Lady_Slippers_in_old_growth_forest_near_a_lake_in_Lunenburg_County%2C_Nova_Scotia%2C_Canada.jpg/500px-Lady_Slippers_in_old_growth_forest_near_a_lake_in_Lunenburg_County%2C_Nova_Scotia%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Lady_Slippers_in_old_growth_forest_near_a_lake_in_Lunenburg_County%2C_Nova_Scotia%2C_Canada.jpg/1280px-Lady_Slippers_in_old_growth_forest_near_a_lake_in_Lunenburg_County%2C_Nova_Scotia%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Lady_Slippers_in_old_growth_forest_near_a_lake_in_Lunenburg_County%2C_Nova_Scotia%2C_Canada.jpg/500px-Lady_Slippers_in_old_growth_forest_near_a_lake_in_Lunenburg_County%2C_Nova_Scotia%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink lady's slippers in Nova Scotia, Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALady_Slippers_in_old_growth_forest_near_a_lake_in_Lunenburg_County%2C_Nova_Scotia%2C_Canada.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Cleaned-Cypripedium_calceolus_guckusko.jpg/330px-Cleaned-Cypripedium_calceolus_guckusko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Cleaned-Cypripedium_calceolus_guckusko.jpg/330px-Cleaned-Cypripedium_calceolus_guckusko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lady's slipper orchid (Cypripedium calceolus)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACleaned-Cypripedium_calceolus_guckus